diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ff92be649ff3f610b38798b3310751534d032814..cd081534092b6a1c21fa42b22092114eed072e69 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,30 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## Features
+
+### JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a [JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901)
+string against a JSON document and returns the value it refers to.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const document = { foo: ['bar', 'baz'] };
+
+resolvePointer(document, '');        // => document
+resolvePointer(document, '/foo/0');  // => 'bar'
+```
+
+It throws when `pointer` is not a syntactically valid JSON Pointer (for example, a non-empty string
+that doesn't start with `/`), or when it does not resolve to a value within `document` — a missing
+member, an out-of-bounds array index, or the `-` array index, which per the RFC never resolves to an
+element.
+
+## Development
+
+- `npm test` runs the test suite.
+- `npm run typecheck` type-checks the source.
+- `npm run build` compiles `src` to `dist`.
